build: 2026-06-30 v10.76.48 (Menu freeze WHILE biofeedback runs — root cause fixed)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Direct fix for "Sobald Biofeedback läuft kann ich nicht mehr in den Dropdown-
  Menüs auswählen." This is the LAST piece of the menu-freeze story — it only happened
  while the camera pulse was active, which earlier (10.76.41/43/47) fixes didn't touch.
  • ROOT CAUSE: the camera fed the pulse analyzer with ONE main-thread task PER FRAME
    (~30/second), submitted from the camera's background queue. That flood of tiny
    main-thread jobs starved the UI, so an open dropdown (Genre/Tonart) stopped
    responding the moment biofeedback ran.
  • FIX: the camera now just drops each frame's 3 colour values into a lock-protected
    buffer (no main-thread hop at all); the existing 10×/s pulse loop empties that buffer
    and feeds the analyzer in one batch on the main thread. Result: 0 per-frame tasks →
    the UI stays free → dropdowns stay selectable WHILE the pulse runs. Frame timestamps
    are carried through so the heart-rate maths is unchanged.
  • ALSO: adaptive refractory for the pulse detector — spaces detected beats at ~½ the
    estimated beat period (0.30–0.60 s) to reject the "dicrotic notch" double-count that
    was inflating BPM on a weak/rounded fingertip signal the other guards couldn't catch.
  Reviewed (concurrency + build): GO, 0 issues. No new sheets / no launch-crash surface.
  Test: 10.76.48 → start the camera pulse (Well), then open Compose ▸ Composition ▸
  Genre/Tonart and change it repeatedly WHILE the pulse is measuring — it must stay open
  and selectable. Pulse BPM should also read truer (no sudden ~1.3–2× jumps on a shaky
  finger). If a dropdown STILL freezes during biofeedback, tell me exactly which menu.
